+## Step-by-Step Operational Guides
+
+### Guide A: Configuring Gemini, OpenAI and Air-Gapped Ollama Providers
+1. Open the AI Providers Studio at `/admin/ai` (or workspace settings at `/workspaces/{ws}/settings`).
+2. Click `+ Register Provider` (`register-provider-btn`) to open the `AiProviderEditorDrawer`.
+3. Choose the provider preset or set `provider_kind`: for Google Gemini, click `Gemini` preset (`preset-gemini-btn`), enter display name `Google Gemini Workspace`, base URL `https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com`, paste API key, click `Probe Models` (`probe-models-btn`) to populate the model list (`gemini-2.5-flash`, `gemini-2.5-pro`), and set timeout ceiling (`15000` to `20000` ms). For OpenAI / Compatible, click `OpenAI` preset (`preset-openai-btn`), enter display name, base URL `https://api.openai.com/v1`, paste API key, and probe or select models (`gpt-4o`, `gpt-4o-mini`). For Local Ollama, click `Ollama` preset (`preset-ollama-btn`), enter display name `Local Ollama Runtime`, base URL `http://127.0.0.1:11434`, residency tier `local_only`, and click `Probe Models` to discover locally hosted models (`llama3.2:latest`, `qwen2.5-coder:latest`). API key is optional for local runtimes.
+4. Expand `Advanced Settings` (`advanced-settings-details`) to adjust temperature (default `0.7`), top-p (default `1.0`), max tokens (default `4096`), and optional mTLS client certificates.
+5. Click `Register Provider` (`save-provider-btn` in create mode, or `Save Provider` when editing existing configs).
+6. Reorder failover priority stack using drag handles or Up/Down buttons (`move-up-btn-{id}`, `move-down-btn-{id}`). The system attempts providers in priority order, falling back cleanly on timeouts or HTTP 5xx errors.
+7. To enforce zero cloud egress, navigate to Workspace Settings and enable `air_gap_mode = true`. Outbound cloud connections and provider create/update attempts for `openai` and `gemini` are rejected with HTTP 409 `AIR_GAP_EGRESS_DENIED` (model probing and connection tests return HTTP 200 with `{"ok": false, "error_code": "AIR_GAP_EGRESS_DENIED", ...}`), while local zero-egress Ollama queries continue without interruption.
+
+### Guide B: Setting Monthly Token Caps and Budget Halting
+1. In `/admin/ai`, locate the target provider card and click `Token Budget` (`manage-budget-btn-{id}`) to open the `AiBudgetModal`.
+2. Select the budget mode: choose Enforce Token Cap (`cap-mode-enforce-btn`) with monthly period and an integer token allowance or preset (`1M`, `5M`, `25M`, `100M`); choose Unlimited Quota (No Cap) (`cap-mode-unlimited-btn`) for an internal cap of `10_000_000_000` tokens; or choose 0 (Freeze) (`preset-budget-0-freeze-btn`) to set monthly cap to `0`, immediately blocking all completion and agent transition requests with `BudgetExceeded` (Sparkle FIM completions return status `budget`).
+3. Click `Save Token Cap` (`save-budget-btn`).
+4. The studio displays real-time progress bars indicating token consumption against the configured ceiling.
+
+### Guide C: Managing Workspace and Project Autonomous Agents
+1. Navigate to Agent Definitions Studio at `/admin/agents` (or project settings `/projects/{proj}/settings/agents`).
+2. Click `+ Register Agent` (`register-agent-btn`) to open the `AgentDefinitionEditorDrawer`.
+3. Fill in agent metadata including slug (lowercase alphanumeric string with hyphens, e.g. `reality-checker`, `security-auditor`), display name, and harness kind (`in_app_sdk`, `cli_pipe`, or `remote_runner`).
+4. Configure harness specifics: for `in_app_sdk`, select `provider_kind` (`gemini`, `openai`, `ollama`) and `model_id`; for `cli_pipe`, select pre-approved binary (`agy` or `codex`) and CLI args (`["-p"]`); for `remote_runner`, select target pool slug (`default`).
+5. Select `repo_access_mode` (`none`, `ro_vfs_mount`, `bare_git_tools`) and check allowed MCP tools (`search_tickets`, `read_ticket`, `search_knowledge`, `read_doc`).
+6. Enter System Instructions in Markdown directing agent persona and verification rules.
+7. Set timeout (`timeout_ms`, default 60000ms, up to 300000ms / 300s).
+8. Click `Save Agent` (`save-agent-btn`).
+9. Click `Test Validation` (`validate-agent-btn-{id}`) to open the `AgentValidationModal`. The system executes a non-destructive test trace and renders a 4-section report (`=== 1. RENDERED CONTEXT ===`, `=== 2. TOOL TRACE ===`, `=== 3. LATENCY & TOKENS ===`, `=== 4. SCHEMA & POLICY STATUS ===`).
+
+### Guide D: Enrolling Non-Root mTLS Runners
+1. Navigate to Remote Runners Studio at `/admin/agent-runners`.
+2. Click `+ Mint Enrollment Token` (`open-mint-modal-btn`) to open the `MintEnrollmentTokenModal`.
+3. Select pool slug (`default`) and token TTL (e.g. 600s, max 900s / 15 minutes), then click `Generate Single-Use Token` (`submit-mint-token-btn`).
+4. Copy the generated enrollment CLI snippet: `echo "$TOKEN" | uv run kanban-agent-runner enroll --server-url https://kanban.example.com --token-stdin --pool default`.
+5. On the runner host, execute the enrollment command as a standard non-root user. The runner daemon generates an EC P-256 private key and CSR (`CN=worker.internal.test`), posts the CSR to `/api/v1/agent-runners/enroll` with the single-use token, receives the signed client certificate (`O=👍kanban Remote Runner Node`), and persists state under strict POSIX file permissions: state directory `0o700` (`drwx------`), `client.key` `0o600`, `ca.pem` `0o600`, and `client.crt` `0o644`.
+6. Start the daemon with `uv run kanban-agent-runner run` (auto-detects runner config) or `uv run kanban-agent-runner run --config ~/.local/state/kanban-runner/runner.toml`.
+7. The runner connects to dedicated mTLS port `:8444` (or WebSocket `/api/v1/agent-runners/ws`), solves the cryptographic Proof-of-Possession challenge `kb-runner-pop-v1:{runner_id}:{nonce}:{cert_sha256}`, and enters `online` state.
+8. To revoke a runner, click `1-Click Revoke (AAL2)` (`POST /api/v1/admin/agent-runners/{id}:revoke`). Reconnection attempts with the revoked certificate are immediately rejected with HTTP 403 Forbidden.
+
+The canonical multi-line enrollment snippet is formatted as:
+```bash
+echo "$TOKEN" | uv run kanban-agent-runner enroll \
+  --server-url https://kanban.example.com \
+  --token-stdin \
+  --pool default
+```
